WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:04.030
- Our next guest is a
Grammy award-winning,

00:00:04.030 --> 00:00:07.430
legendary music icon whose contributions

00:00:07.430 --> 00:00:10.970
to art and music and culture span decades.

00:00:10.970 --> 00:00:13.680
Thanks to her, we've been on our feet

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:16.740
and catching the rhythm
and doing the conga

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:18.370
for the last 40 years.

00:00:18.370 --> 00:00:22.743
Please welcome the
glorious Gloria Estefan.

00:00:22.743 --> 00:00:25.272
(audience claps)
- Oh.

00:00:25.272 --> 00:00:26.653
My gosh.

00:00:26.653 --> 00:00:27.824
- Oh my-
- What a warming

00:00:27.824 --> 00:00:29.210
introduction.

00:00:29.210 --> 00:00:32.320
And I'm a huge fan of yours,
Drew, by the way, hello.

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:34.390
- I love you so much.
- We all are.

00:00:34.390 --> 00:00:37.674
- And by the way, you look so beautiful.

00:00:37.674 --> 00:00:39.482
- Oh, thank you so much.

00:00:39.482 --> 00:00:41.940
And what a privilege to be on your show.

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:43.820
- There's so much to celebrate.

00:00:43.820 --> 00:00:46.180
We're having a hard time figuring out,

00:00:46.180 --> 00:00:48.280
like, which subject to prioritize

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:52.360
of your incredibly multi-diverse life.

00:00:52.360 --> 00:00:55.880
One of the things was that you had said,

00:00:55.880 --> 00:01:00.440
I believe, that your 40s were
one of your favorite decades?

00:01:00.440 --> 00:01:02.117
- Yes, absolutely.

00:01:02.117 --> 00:01:04.848
You know, when people say,
"Oh no, I'm turning 40,"

00:01:04.848 --> 00:01:07.177
especially women, okay, I tell them,

00:01:07.177 --> 00:01:08.440
"That's my favorite decade."

00:01:08.440 --> 00:01:09.310
It was...

00:01:09.310 --> 00:01:10.893
You know, you're still hot.

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:14.570
My body was on point
'cause I'd been working out

00:01:14.570 --> 00:01:18.240
so much after that accident
too, and I got a little miracle

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:20.240
when I was 37, that they had told me

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:22.030
I'd never be able to have another baby

00:01:22.030 --> 00:01:23.590
and I had my daughter, Emily.

00:01:23.590 --> 00:01:26.180
So it was the best years of my life.

00:01:26.180 --> 00:01:29.471
I actually took time off from touring

00:01:29.471 --> 00:01:31.230
to be able to go to her games

00:01:31.230 --> 00:01:33.370
'cause she was an amazing
basketball player,

00:01:33.370 --> 00:01:36.501
starting in 5th grade,
and she was a musician

00:01:36.501 --> 00:01:39.570
and I would go to all her
shows and take her to school.

00:01:39.570 --> 00:01:41.370
We took her to school
every day, Emilio and I,

00:01:41.370 --> 00:01:42.900
and I picked her up.

00:01:42.900 --> 00:01:45.147
So I really, I had the luxury at that time

00:01:45.147 --> 00:01:47.835
to be able to really
choose what I wanted to do.

00:01:47.835 --> 00:01:49.864
But yeah, 40s were magnificent,

00:01:49.864 --> 00:01:51.950
and every, every decade's been great

00:01:51.950 --> 00:01:54.430
'cause I always say you're
either older or dead.

00:01:54.430 --> 00:01:55.950
- Yeah.
- So I'll take

00:01:55.950 --> 00:01:57.470
whatever comes with it.

00:01:57.470 --> 00:02:00.109
- The reason I love hearing
you talk about your 40s

00:02:00.109 --> 00:02:03.969
with, you know, a beautiful
reverie and positivity

00:02:03.969 --> 00:02:07.442
is I'm smack dab in the
middle of them right now.

00:02:07.442 --> 00:02:09.130
and this decade,
- Yes.

00:02:09.130 --> 00:02:11.620
Without question, has
been the best of my life.

00:02:11.620 --> 00:02:15.580
And I'm glad that we were
able to have these life paths

00:02:15.580 --> 00:02:18.512
where we can focus on work
and then take time off

00:02:18.512 --> 00:02:22.890
when we had our kids, and
that's such a blessing

00:02:22.890 --> 00:02:25.793
and it is a luxury.
- It is a luxury.

00:02:25.793 --> 00:02:27.960
It's a luxury, and not many women

00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:30.203
can take their kids to work, which I did

00:02:30.203 --> 00:02:32.345
because I was on tour all over the world.

00:02:32.345 --> 00:02:36.480
And when Emily was two, we went on tour

00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:41.123
with my then 16-year-old
son and her at two.

00:02:41.123 --> 00:02:44.100
And they'd see their mom
bigger than life on that stage

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:46.560
and then want to spend time after.

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:48.710
Then I became Mommy after the show.

00:02:48.710 --> 00:02:51.640
And it's a great grounding
and beautiful experience

00:02:51.640 --> 00:02:53.109
and I wouldn't have had it any other way.

00:02:53.109 --> 00:02:54.259
(audience claps)
- Oh my gosh.

00:02:54.259 --> 00:02:56.190
Talking to you is such an inspiration.

00:02:56.190 --> 00:03:00.570
And your husband, Emilio,
you guys married in 1978?

00:03:00.570 --> 00:03:01.770
- Yes, indeed.

00:03:01.770 --> 00:03:03.770
We've been married 42 years.

00:03:03.770 --> 00:03:06.680
45 together. The first
one, he was my boss.

00:03:06.680 --> 00:03:07.920
Yeah, it's been great.

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:09.490
I am a blessed woman.

00:03:09.490 --> 00:03:11.550
He is a feminist.

00:03:11.550 --> 00:03:15.624
He's the most incredibly supportive man,

00:03:15.624 --> 00:03:18.100
and to everyone, he's a motivator.

00:03:18.100 --> 00:03:19.566
He gets up every day raring to go

00:03:19.566 --> 00:03:21.990
and he finds new things to do

00:03:21.990 --> 00:03:25.480
and still recording this amazing album

00:03:25.480 --> 00:03:26.835
for The Wailers this year

00:03:26.835 --> 00:03:29.200
and he's working on music constantly,

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:31.930
makes my life as easy
as he can every moment,

00:03:31.930 --> 00:03:34.670
and he's just a lovable
guy, and very funny.

00:03:34.670 --> 00:03:36.430
He makes me laugh every day of my life.

00:03:36.430 --> 00:03:37.910
He's really an amazing guy.

00:03:37.910 --> 00:03:41.780
- I think, if there's a way to, like,

00:03:41.780 --> 00:03:44.210
subconsciously submerge ourselves

00:03:44.210 --> 00:03:49.050
in all men's minds right now,
I do believe a secret way

00:03:49.050 --> 00:03:52.660
into a woman's heart is humor, 100%.

00:03:52.660 --> 00:03:53.640
- Yes.

00:03:53.640 --> 00:03:58.640
- And a daily kindness, I think,
just goes the longest way.

00:03:59.160 --> 00:04:02.670
And I know that you're
doing the Red Table Talks

00:04:02.670 --> 00:04:04.160
with your niece, Lili,
- Yes.

00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:05.260
- and your daughter, Emily.

00:04:05.260 --> 00:04:07.950
And when we come back, I
want to talk about this

00:04:07.950 --> 00:04:12.439
because I am so excited for this

00:04:12.439 --> 00:04:17.439
for all of us that I just
can't wait to dive in.

00:04:18.420 --> 00:04:23.420
And when you are able to
share the life journey

00:04:23.780 --> 00:04:27.330
with other people so that
other people don't feel alone

00:04:27.330 --> 00:04:29.500
and we can benefit from
each other's wisdom

00:04:29.500 --> 00:04:32.447
and there's a diversity within
your family of experiences.

00:04:32.447 --> 00:04:35.030
(upbeat music)

